  :adr/topic "incidence-first-individual"
  :adr/title "Individual is a basis-scoped incidence quotient; DID is a binding"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-08-12"
  :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :adr/related ["DoDAF 2.02" "W3C DID Core 1.0" "com-junkawasaki/inc"]
  :adr/body
  "## Decision

EAF has one primitive architectural element: incidence. An individual is the
observational quotient of a scoped incidence closure at an immutable basis.
Raw IDs do not establish equality, and cross-basis continuity is not inferred.

DID binding, authentication occurrence, session principal, authorization,
and execution identity are distinct incidences. A valid authentication proof
does not authorize an effect. Effectful execution requires an individual,
authentication occurrence, and constrained authority incidence; pure
computation may be anonymous.

All viewpoints are deterministic projections from the same canonical graph.
They do not own independent copies of architecture facts.

## R0 representation choice

The current Inc Lean core requires endpoint type consistency. R0 therefore
uses one common carrier and expresses semantic kinds through
`:incidence/kind`. A future heterogeneous dependent boundary must provide an
erasure into this carrier and prove preservation before replacing it."}]
